WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.560
You know, usually when we talk about a system working perfectly, there is this, like, expectation of total control.

00:07.860 --> 00:08.420
Oh, absolutely.

00:08.980 --> 00:11.380
Think about the feeling of driving a highly responsive car.

00:11.960 --> 00:16.160
Like, you slide into the driver's seat, you grip the steering wheel, you press the accelerator,

00:16.160 --> 00:21.300
and the vehicle just executes your physical commands flawlessly.

00:21.980 --> 00:23.340
Right. It does exactly what you want.

00:23.480 --> 00:27.020
Yeah. It turns exactly when you want it to turn.

00:27.380 --> 00:29.500
It stops exactly when you want it to stop.

00:29.500 --> 00:33.460
It is a profoundly satisfying feeling, that kind of responsiveness.

00:34.020 --> 00:39.120
I mean, it creates this seamless feedback loop between your intention and the machine's action.

00:39.360 --> 00:39.660
Yeah.

00:40.060 --> 00:43.220
And that immediate obedience gives you a deep sense of mastery.

00:43.220 --> 00:48.940
You feel quite literally in the driver's seat, like you are the absolute author of the journey.

00:49.140 --> 00:53.280
But I want you to imagine a slightly different scenario.

00:53.760 --> 00:54.120
Okay.

00:54.120 --> 01:00.060
Imagine you're in that exact same car, and you are driving down a complex, winding highway.

01:00.240 --> 01:04.340
You're navigating traffic with, you know, absolute, flawless precision.

01:04.740 --> 01:05.520
So you're doing great.

01:05.660 --> 01:05.860
Right.

01:06.260 --> 01:07.740
Your reaction times are perfect.

01:08.200 --> 01:13.860
You are merging smoothly, hitting the brakes at just the right moment, accelerating into the open lanes.

01:13.900 --> 01:15.200
You're doing an incredible job.

01:15.540 --> 01:15.820
Uh-huh.

01:15.820 --> 01:21.820
But then, an hour into the drive, a terrifying realization washes over you.

01:22.640 --> 01:25.180
You never actually entered a destination into the GPS.

01:26.440 --> 01:26.980
Oh, wow.

01:27.460 --> 01:28.800
Yeah, you didn't pick where you're going.

01:29.320 --> 01:34.920
And worse, as you look at the dashboard and the locked doors, you realize you can't find a way to pull over.

01:35.280 --> 01:36.320
You're just stuck driving.

01:36.760 --> 01:37.140
Exactly.

01:37.660 --> 01:39.780
You are flawlessly executing a journey.

01:39.780 --> 01:42.640
You're hitting every single metric for safe, efficient driving.

01:42.800 --> 01:46.560
But you have entirely lost control over the actual purpose of the trip.

01:47.180 --> 01:52.060
The car is like using your reflexes to get somewhere, but it's not somewhere you chose.

01:52.640 --> 01:59.300
That image, that flawless driver trapped in a destinationless, or rather an externally determined journey.

01:59.480 --> 02:02.480
That is the absolute definition of a captured delegation.

02:02.840 --> 02:03.780
It's spooky, right?

02:03.980 --> 02:05.160
It is deeply unsettling.

02:05.380 --> 02:05.500
Yeah.

02:06.320 --> 02:09.680
But it is precisely the structural reality we are looking at today.

02:10.280 --> 02:15.800
It describes the hidden architecture of a vast number of our modern professional, civic, and even personal lives.

02:16.140 --> 02:18.440
So, welcome everyone to this deep dive.

02:18.840 --> 02:21.320
Today, we are taking you on a very specific mission.

02:21.500 --> 02:21.840
Yes, we are.

02:22.100 --> 02:25.420
Our goal is to understand the mechanics of that exact trap.

02:25.720 --> 02:32.580
Like, how is it entirely possible for you to perfectly execute your tasks, hit all of your key performance indicators,

02:32.580 --> 02:40.580
generate incredible economic or social benefits, and yet somehow completely lose control over the ultimate purpose of your work?

02:40.680 --> 02:40.920
Right.

02:40.960 --> 02:41.580
How does that happen?

02:41.580 --> 02:51.180
We really want to unpack how human agency, our actual ability to choose our own ends, gets quietly captured by the very systems we believe we are running.

02:51.180 --> 02:57.140
And to crack this wide open, we have an incredibly dense, rewarding piece of source material to guide us today.

02:57.460 --> 02:58.000
Oh, definitely.

02:58.000 --> 03:04.380
We are examining an October 2026 paper by an independent researcher who publishes under the name Fleixion.

03:05.060 --> 03:09.740
The paper is titled, Nietzsche, Delegated Agency, and the Admissibility of Ends.

03:09.740 --> 03:14.020
Now, I have to admit, when I first saw that title, I braced myself a little bit.

03:14.200 --> 03:14.900
I mean, fair enough.

03:15.020 --> 03:26.380
Yeah, because seeing the name Nietzsche parked next to phrases like admissibility of ends usually signals a plunge into very dry, very abstract, philosophical navel gazing.

03:26.600 --> 03:27.580
It sounds like a tough read.

03:27.580 --> 03:32.580
But, having spent time with this research, I can promise you, it is anything but that.

03:32.980 --> 03:41.140
This paper is a rigorous, mathematical, and structural breakdown of how traps are built around human choices.

03:41.360 --> 03:42.620
Yeah, it's incredibly grounded.

03:43.100 --> 03:43.340
Right.

03:43.440 --> 03:50.580
It actually uses graph theory, formal logic, and econometrics to literally map out the exact geometry of how we lose our autonomy.

03:51.140 --> 03:55.640
And what is genuinely fascinating about this paper is its central premise.

03:56.060 --> 03:56.300
Okay.

03:56.300 --> 03:57.380
Let's get into that.

03:57.580 --> 04:05.120
Fleixion takes a set of concepts that we normally almost automatically kind of fuse together in our minds and just kind of brutally separates them.

04:05.600 --> 04:05.840
Like what?

04:06.420 --> 04:19.460
Well, in our everyday lives, we tend to assume that if a system works smoothly, if the people operating it are highly competent, and if it produces a lot of tangible benefits, then the overarching goals of that system must be legitimate.

04:19.720 --> 04:19.920
Right.

04:19.980 --> 04:20.800
We just assume that.

04:21.000 --> 04:21.360
Exactly.

04:21.760 --> 04:25.060
We treat operational competence as evidence of underlying consent.

04:25.060 --> 04:33.140
But this paper proves, using actual mathematical theorems, that this assumption is one of the most dangerous traps in modern society.

04:33.140 --> 04:38.860
Okay, so let's start pulling this apart, because I think we need to look at exactly how we conflate those ideas.

04:39.420 --> 04:42.120
I was actually thinking about this in the context of building a house.

04:42.360 --> 04:42.600
Okay.

04:42.780 --> 04:43.020
Yeah.

04:43.020 --> 04:49.800
So let's say you hire a master carpenter, they get the blueprints, and they execute the build flawlessly.

04:50.180 --> 04:51.440
Perfect joints, everything.

04:51.440 --> 04:52.100
Exactly.

04:52.280 --> 04:56.320
The joints are perfectly flushed, the foundation is solid, the framing is immaculate.

04:57.020 --> 05:03.340
The carpenter didn't decide if the building should be a family home, a commercial bakery, or a massive corporate warehouse.

05:03.480 --> 05:05.260
They just executed the plans they were handed.

05:05.520 --> 05:05.720
Right.

05:06.240 --> 05:10.180
Now, in a normal, healthy division of labor, that is completely fine.

05:10.580 --> 05:13.560
The client chose the purpose, and the carpenter supplied the execution.

05:14.060 --> 05:16.280
We need that to function as a society.

05:16.280 --> 05:17.740
We do.

05:18.060 --> 05:26.560
I mean, if every single worker had to philosophically re-derive and authorize the ultimate purpose of every single task they performed, the world would just grind to a halt.

05:26.680 --> 05:26.800
Right.

05:26.880 --> 05:27.560
Nothing would get done.

05:27.840 --> 05:28.140
Exactly.

05:28.560 --> 05:32.740
The air traffic controller doesn't need to debate the existential validity of a passenger's vacation.

05:33.060 --> 05:34.520
They just need to land the plane safely.

05:35.420 --> 05:37.680
Division of labor inherently depends on delegation.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.760
Flyxion acknowledges this right up front.

05:41.120 --> 05:45.180
There is nothing inherently malicious about executing an end chosen by someone else.

05:45.180 --> 05:45.680
Right.

05:46.280 --> 05:47.780
So where does the trap actually spring?

05:48.020 --> 05:51.160
If the carpenter building the house is fine, when does it become a problem?

05:51.580 --> 05:58.260
The difficulty begins when we start making a very specific, incredibly common, but logically flawed inference.

05:59.000 --> 05:59.520
Which is?

05:59.520 --> 06:10.660
We look at the highly skilled executor, like your master carpenter, or maybe a brilliant algorithmic software engineer, or a highly efficient human resources manager, and we observe the outcome.

06:11.340 --> 06:11.600
Uh-huh.

06:11.600 --> 06:14.680
We say, wow, this arrangement works really well.

06:14.980 --> 06:15.780
It's efficient.

06:16.140 --> 06:16.880
It's profitable.

06:17.680 --> 06:21.160
Then without realizing it, we take a massive logical leap.

06:21.480 --> 06:26.840
We say, because this arrangement works so well, its foundational purposes must be sound.

06:27.340 --> 06:28.000
Oh, I see.

06:28.000 --> 06:31.160
And then we take the final fatal step.

06:31.740 --> 06:39.740
Because the purposes are sound, questioning them is unnecessary, and eventually questioning them becomes improper.

06:39.740 --> 06:42.400
Or even a fireable offense.

06:42.400 --> 06:49.580
So we let the sheer skill of the carpenter act as retroactive proof that the building should have been built in the first place.

06:49.980 --> 06:50.400
Exactly.

06:50.400 --> 07:03.880
Or, to bring it to the modern workplace, we let the fact that an algorithm is incredibly good at keeping teenagers glued to a screen serve as proof that keeping teenagers glued to a screen is a fundamentally good and authorized goal.

07:04.420 --> 07:04.960
Precisely.

07:05.540 --> 07:10.820
Each step in that logical chain is illicitly borrowing credit from a completely different achievement.

07:10.820 --> 07:20.360
And that is why Flicendian spends the opening of the paper separating out four distinct achievements that society constantly, dangerously runs together.

07:21.060 --> 07:24.700
We have to look at these four categories to understand how the trap works.

07:25.380 --> 07:26.320
Okay, let's lay them out.

07:26.560 --> 07:29.320
If we are constantly mixing these up, we need to define the boundaries.

07:29.840 --> 07:33.620
The first achievement the paper identifies is reliable execution.

07:33.620 --> 07:36.300
This is exactly what it sounds like.

07:36.900 --> 07:43.300
It is simply the ability of an agent or a system to carry out a specified purpose with a very low error rate.

07:43.480 --> 07:44.120
Like the pilot.

07:44.660 --> 07:46.380
Right, the pilot landing the plane in bad weather.

07:46.940 --> 07:49.620
The surgeon performing a complex bypass.

07:50.320 --> 07:52.600
It is purely about competence in action.

07:52.720 --> 07:53.520
It is the how.

07:53.900 --> 07:54.220
Okay.

07:54.700 --> 07:56.100
Execution is the how.

07:57.100 --> 07:59.620
The second achievement is beneficial consequence.

07:59.960 --> 08:01.720
I imagine this is the scoreboard?

08:02.160 --> 08:02.680
Exactly.

08:02.680 --> 08:08.940
This is the degree to which the outcomes of the execution are considered good by some stated measure.

08:09.700 --> 08:11.040
Does the system produce wealth?

08:11.480 --> 08:12.380
Does it cure disease?

08:13.020 --> 08:15.420
Does it maximize a specific utility function?

08:15.820 --> 08:19.540
It is the measurable output, the points on the board.

08:19.900 --> 08:20.020
Right.

08:20.960 --> 08:23.620
And the third achievement is organizational endurance.

08:24.240 --> 08:27.240
This one is vital and often overlooked.

08:28.040 --> 08:30.660
Endurance is simply the persistence of an arrangement over time.

08:30.660 --> 08:32.340
Does the system survive?

08:32.680 --> 08:36.000
Can it reproduce the conditions necessary for its own existence?

08:36.400 --> 08:38.020
And longevity doesn't mean it's good.

08:38.600 --> 08:39.020
Exactly.

08:39.740 --> 08:41.040
Here is the kicker.

08:41.040 --> 08:50.640
A highly toxic, damaging bureaucracy might have incredible organizational endurance simply because it has successfully made it impossible for anyone to dismantle it.

08:50.640 --> 08:51.640
Survival does not equal morality.

08:51.640 --> 08:53.260
Survival does not equal morality.

08:53.820 --> 08:55.680
And endurance does not equal legitimacy.

08:55.680 --> 08:57.080
That makes a lot of sense.

08:57.460 --> 09:01.700
Like, just because a bad corporate policy has been around for 20 years doesn't mean it's good.

09:01.820 --> 09:03.660
It just means it's heavily defended.

09:03.940 --> 09:04.040
Right.

09:04.440 --> 09:09.100
Which brings us to the fourth achievement, the one that the paper argues is the most critical.

09:09.860 --> 09:11.520
Legitimate purpose setting.

09:11.520 --> 09:13.660
This is the core of human agency.

09:14.380 --> 09:25.020
Legitimate purpose setting is the standing, the recognized, authorized authority of a particular party or process to actually select the ends that the arrangement serves.

09:25.480 --> 09:27.200
Who actually gets to choose.

09:27.200 --> 09:27.680
Exactly.

09:28.220 --> 09:38.600
And crucially, Flyxion insists that this achievement must include the continuing ability of the affected parties to examine, contest, and revise that selection over time.

09:38.720 --> 09:40.160
It's not just a one-time vote.

09:40.380 --> 09:42.620
It's an ongoing capacity for revision.

09:42.620 --> 09:50.840
Okay, so we have reliable execution, beneficial consequence, organizational endurance, and legitimate purpose setting.

09:51.220 --> 09:57.840
And the central thesis here is that you can have the first three in absolute spades while completely lacking the fourth.

09:58.000 --> 09:59.600
That is the terrifying reality.

10:00.160 --> 10:06.400
You can find yourself inside a system that executes flawlessly, generates massive, record-breaking benefits,

10:06.400 --> 10:13.400
and has endured for decades, all while operating under a purpose that absolutely nobody legitimately agreed to.

10:14.340 --> 10:16.880
And with no mechanism for anyone to ever change it.

10:17.000 --> 10:17.160
Right.

10:17.620 --> 10:21.420
And the illusion is that the presence of the first three silently supplies the fourth.

10:22.140 --> 10:28.660
We assume that because the system is surviving and profiting, someone somewhere must have legitimately authorized it.

10:29.080 --> 10:34.680
Which introduces what I think is the most striking, memorable piece of terminology in this entire paper.

10:34.680 --> 10:37.540
The concept of the reverse centaur.

10:37.860 --> 10:40.700
Let's dig into this because this image really stayed with me.

10:41.140 --> 10:46.180
To fully grasp the reverse centaur, we first have to understand the original centaur concept.

10:46.800 --> 10:52.400
This term gained popularity in the world of advanced chess, particularly in the late 1990s,

10:52.700 --> 10:56.400
after Garry Kasparov famously lost to IBM's Deep Blue supercomputer.

10:56.840 --> 10:57.220
Right.

10:57.460 --> 10:58.420
That was a huge moment.

10:58.620 --> 10:58.980
It was.

10:58.980 --> 11:04.940
So after that defeat, the chess world experimented with a new format called Advanced Chess,

11:05.200 --> 11:09.300
where a human player competes while using computer assistants.

11:09.580 --> 11:11.460
So it's not human versus machine.

11:11.580 --> 11:12.440
It's a hybrid team.

11:12.660 --> 11:12.880
Right.

11:13.540 --> 11:16.700
In this setup, the machine does what it does best.

11:17.040 --> 11:19.400
It calculates millions of possible moves,

11:19.880 --> 11:21.160
checks tactical combinations,

11:21.160 --> 11:23.480
and ensures there are no immediate blunders.

11:23.480 --> 11:27.240
But the human being sets the overarching strategy,

11:27.820 --> 11:29.300
determines the style of play,

11:29.800 --> 11:31.860
and dictates the ultimate purpose of the game.

11:32.480 --> 11:33.560
So the human is in charge.

11:33.880 --> 11:34.260
Exactly.

11:34.900 --> 11:36.860
The human is augmented by the machine.

11:37.400 --> 11:38.400
The human is the head,

11:38.740 --> 11:40.620
and the machine is the powerful body.

11:41.060 --> 11:42.080
That is a centaur.

11:42.300 --> 11:44.060
The human is still in charge of the destination.

11:44.280 --> 11:47.180
They just have a much faster, stronger engine to get there.

11:47.300 --> 11:50.760
But a reverse centaur flips that entire dynamic on its head.

11:50.760 --> 11:52.960
It is the exact opposite role structure.

11:53.940 --> 11:55.160
In a reverse centaur arrangement,

11:55.360 --> 11:57.780
the human being is reduced to a mere actuator.

11:58.080 --> 11:58.900
Like a part of the machine.

11:59.220 --> 11:59.580
Exactly.

12:00.380 --> 12:02.320
The human serves the pace, the metrics,

12:02.520 --> 12:05.760
and the overarching goals of an external controller.

12:06.360 --> 12:09.600
The machine, or the bureaucratic system, is the head.

12:10.180 --> 12:12.820
It determines what needs to be done and how fast.

12:13.540 --> 12:16.200
The human is just the physical hands carrying out the work,

12:16.680 --> 12:20.080
often because it's still cheaper or more dexterous to use human hands

12:20.080 --> 12:21.680
than to build a fully autonomous robot.

12:22.140 --> 12:24.600
I see this everywhere now.

12:25.160 --> 12:27.400
Think about warehouse workers who wear headsets

12:27.400 --> 12:29.720
that literally count down the seconds they have

12:29.720 --> 12:31.120
to walk to a specific shelf,

12:31.580 --> 12:32.640
pick up a specific item,

12:32.760 --> 12:33.760
and place it in a bin.

12:34.040 --> 12:34.260
Yes.

12:34.260 --> 12:36.580
The algorithm calculated the optimal path.

12:36.960 --> 12:39.260
The algorithm determined the priority of the package.

12:39.840 --> 12:42.840
And the human being is simply the biological forklift

12:42.840 --> 12:43.940
executing the move.

12:44.360 --> 12:46.180
You are doing the physical labor.

12:46.620 --> 12:47.880
You are in the loop.

12:47.880 --> 12:50.420
You might even be making tiny micro decisions

12:50.420 --> 12:51.880
about how to grip the box.

12:52.060 --> 12:54.080
But you have exactly zero control

12:54.080 --> 12:55.840
over the ultimate purpose you are serving.

12:56.280 --> 12:59.740
That is a perfect, visceral example of a reverse centaur.

13:00.520 --> 13:02.080
But Flyxion takes it a step further.

13:02.740 --> 13:05.320
It is crucial to understand that the external controller

13:05.320 --> 13:07.900
doesn't have to be a computer algorithm or a piece of software.

13:08.400 --> 13:09.120
What else could it be?

13:09.380 --> 13:11.280
It could be a sprawling corporate bureaucracy.

13:11.960 --> 13:14.360
It could be a rigid set of key performance indicators

13:14.360 --> 13:16.140
that dictate every hour of your workday.

13:16.800 --> 13:17.580
It could even be,

13:18.180 --> 13:20.120
and this is where it gets really philosophical,

13:20.920 --> 13:22.560
an authoritative moral doctrine.

13:23.360 --> 13:23.780
Hold on.

13:24.760 --> 13:25.900
A moral doctrine.

13:26.060 --> 13:29.060
I mean, I understand being a reverse centaur

13:29.060 --> 13:30.760
to an Amazon algorithm,

13:30.900 --> 13:32.580
but how can you be a reverse centaur

13:32.580 --> 13:33.740
to a moral concept?

13:34.420 --> 13:35.440
Think about it structurally.

13:35.440 --> 13:37.500
You can have human beings sitting

13:37.500 --> 13:39.060
in every single node of an arrangement.

13:39.780 --> 13:41.420
Humans are making all the physical moves.

13:41.740 --> 13:42.940
Humans are having the conversations.

13:43.540 --> 13:44.580
Humans are doing all the labor.

13:45.140 --> 13:46.860
But they are doing it in strict obedience

13:46.860 --> 13:49.260
to a doctrine that they have no power to alter.

13:50.000 --> 13:51.640
So the doctrine is the boss.

13:52.060 --> 13:52.280
Yes.

13:52.640 --> 13:54.280
They are simply servicing the doctrine.

13:54.860 --> 13:55.760
They are its hands.

13:56.360 --> 13:57.980
You can have a fully human system

13:57.980 --> 13:58.960
without a single human

13:58.960 --> 14:00.900
actually authoring the system's ends.

14:00.900 --> 14:03.640
That is a wild,

14:03.820 --> 14:05.460
almost disturbing thing to think about

14:05.460 --> 14:07.920
because when you are in that position,

14:08.100 --> 14:10.600
you probably feel incredibly engaged in your work.

14:10.740 --> 14:11.280
You're busy.

14:11.500 --> 14:13.200
You feel necessary to the operation.

14:14.040 --> 14:16.740
And you might completely mistake

14:16.740 --> 14:18.320
that intense feeling of involvement

14:18.320 --> 14:20.300
for actual authority.

14:20.800 --> 14:20.920
Right.

14:21.080 --> 14:21.980
You think you're in charge.

14:22.280 --> 14:23.240
You think you're driving the car

14:23.240 --> 14:24.360
because your hands are on the wheel,

14:24.540 --> 14:26.340
but you're really just the engine block.

14:26.700 --> 14:27.040
Exactly.

14:27.460 --> 14:29.020
And there is a fascinating parallel

14:29.020 --> 14:31.380
in the human factors engineering literature

14:31.380 --> 14:32.760
that Flyoxian points out.

14:33.180 --> 14:35.680
They call it a moral crumple zone.

14:36.120 --> 14:37.100
Moral crumple zone.

14:37.280 --> 14:37.460
Yeah.

14:37.580 --> 14:38.740
It's a neighboring pattern

14:38.740 --> 14:40.200
where human operators

14:40.200 --> 14:42.380
of highly complex automated systems

14:42.380 --> 14:44.360
retain all the moral

14:44.360 --> 14:45.480
and legal responsibility

14:45.480 --> 14:46.320
for a system

14:46.320 --> 14:48.580
that they can no longer meaningfully control.

14:49.580 --> 14:50.760
If the autopilot fails,

14:51.000 --> 14:52.380
the human pilot takes the blame.

14:53.040 --> 14:54.060
You get all the liability

14:54.060 --> 14:55.260
if the execution fails,

14:55.760 --> 14:57.720
but you had absolutely no say

14:57.720 --> 14:59.280
in the purpose you were executing.

15:00.060 --> 15:01.320
The human absorbs the impact.

15:02.120 --> 15:03.060
Man, that's heavy.

15:03.820 --> 15:05.860
Okay, so if we can become reverse centaurs,

15:06.040 --> 15:07.040
not just to technology,

15:07.220 --> 15:08.580
but to abstract concepts

15:08.580 --> 15:09.680
like corporate metrics

15:09.680 --> 15:11.020
or moral doctrines,

15:11.580 --> 15:12.320
we need to ask,

15:12.440 --> 15:13.860
how does that actually happen?

15:14.520 --> 15:15.800
People generally don't wake up

15:15.800 --> 15:16.500
in the morning and say,

15:16.600 --> 15:17.840
I'd love to be a mindless

15:17.840 --> 15:19.080
biological actuator

15:19.080 --> 15:20.400
for a system I don't control.

15:20.860 --> 15:21.980
How do we drift into this?

15:22.660 --> 15:23.900
To explain the mechanics

15:23.900 --> 15:25.180
of how a person becomes

15:25.180 --> 15:26.280
a flawless instrument

15:26.280 --> 15:27.560
for an unchosen purpose,

15:27.560 --> 15:29.800
the paper takes a very interesting

15:29.800 --> 15:31.460
genealogical point of departure.

15:32.160 --> 15:34.240
It goes back to the 19th century philosopher

15:34.240 --> 15:35.420
Friedrich Nietzsche.

15:36.140 --> 15:36.720
Ah, Nietzsche.

15:37.280 --> 15:37.820
Specifically,

15:38.280 --> 15:39.400
Phlyoxian examines

15:39.400 --> 15:40.680
structural observations

15:40.680 --> 15:41.980
found in Nietzsche's notes,

15:42.460 --> 15:44.020
compiled in The Will to Power,

15:44.640 --> 15:46.960
specifically passages 354,

15:47.180 --> 15:48.660
356, and 358,

15:49.120 --> 15:50.100
as well as passages

15:50.100 --> 15:52.080
from The Genealogy of Morals

15:52.080 --> 15:53.860
and Twilight of the Idols.

15:53.860 --> 15:55.520
Now, I want to pause right here

15:55.520 --> 15:57.180
and offer a very clear caveat

15:57.180 --> 15:58.300
for you listening.

15:59.240 --> 16:00.460
Whenever Nietzsche is brought up,

16:00.560 --> 16:02.600
he brings a massive amount

16:02.600 --> 16:04.380
of historical and political baggage

16:04.380 --> 16:05.000
into the room.

16:05.520 --> 16:07.360
He held some highly hierarchical,

16:07.660 --> 16:07.960
aggressive,

16:08.180 --> 16:08.680
and frankly,

16:08.880 --> 16:09.760
very controversial

16:09.760 --> 16:11.120
political prescriptions.

16:11.540 --> 16:12.080
Very much so.

16:12.380 --> 16:13.260
But the paper makes

16:13.260 --> 16:14.740
a strict, explicit point

16:14.740 --> 16:16.540
of scholarly impartiality here.

16:16.760 --> 16:17.860
We are not looking

16:17.860 --> 16:18.900
at Nietzsche's politics.

16:19.280 --> 16:20.240
We are strictly looking

16:20.240 --> 16:21.740
at his structural diagnosis

16:21.740 --> 16:23.780
of how morality functions.

16:24.220 --> 16:24.940
It's like looking at

16:24.940 --> 16:26.260
a controversial architect's

16:26.260 --> 16:27.220
blueprint for a bridge,

16:27.280 --> 16:27.520
you know?

16:27.640 --> 16:28.560
We are just examining

16:28.560 --> 16:29.700
the load-bearing math

16:29.700 --> 16:30.480
of the arches,

16:30.740 --> 16:31.660
not endorsing

16:31.660 --> 16:32.640
the architect's worldview.

16:33.400 --> 16:34.340
Yes, that distinction

16:34.340 --> 16:35.360
is absolutely vital.

16:35.820 --> 16:36.560
We are extracting

16:36.560 --> 16:37.840
a mechanical observation.

16:38.440 --> 16:39.160
In those passages

16:39.160 --> 16:40.200
of The Will to Power,

16:40.720 --> 16:41.400
Nietzsche describes

16:41.400 --> 16:43.680
how a particular moral ideal

16:43.680 --> 16:44.860
can functionally

16:44.860 --> 16:45.940
take over a person.

16:46.520 --> 16:47.320
He points out that

16:47.320 --> 16:47.960
virtues,

16:48.220 --> 16:49.360
things we universally

16:49.360 --> 16:50.900
consider inherently good,

16:50.900 --> 16:52.400
like being industrious,

16:52.820 --> 16:53.580
being benevolent,

16:53.960 --> 16:54.600
being temperate,

16:54.640 --> 16:55.940
or being a hard worker.

16:56.500 --> 16:57.580
They can actually function

16:57.580 --> 16:58.940
as the exact mechanisms

16:58.940 --> 17:00.140
that make a person

17:00.140 --> 17:01.660
highly useful to ends

17:01.660 --> 17:03.020
that they cannot establish

17:03.020 --> 17:03.660
for themselves.

17:04.420 --> 17:05.500
I really want to push back

17:05.500 --> 17:06.420
on this because it feels

17:06.420 --> 17:07.860
completely counterintuitive.

17:08.420 --> 17:09.120
Are you saying that

17:09.120 --> 17:10.060
being a hard worker,

17:10.460 --> 17:11.180
being industrious,

17:11.260 --> 17:13.100
which literally every parent

17:13.100 --> 17:14.320
teaches their child to be,

17:14.680 --> 17:16.460
can actually be the exact trait

17:16.460 --> 17:17.960
that springs the trap?

17:18.280 --> 17:19.360
Isn't being industrious

17:19.360 --> 17:21.180
just objectively good?

17:21.180 --> 17:23.360
It is good for execution,

17:23.880 --> 17:24.500
but structurally,

17:24.860 --> 17:26.980
if you are incredibly industrious,

17:27.360 --> 17:28.940
you are a fantastic,

17:29.200 --> 17:30.280
highly efficient tool

17:30.280 --> 17:31.740
for someone else's purpose.

17:32.660 --> 17:34.040
Nietzsche's structural observation

17:34.040 --> 17:35.240
is that the language

17:35.240 --> 17:35.980
of morality

17:35.980 --> 17:37.860
can render this subordination

17:37.860 --> 17:39.380
entirely self-justifying.

17:40.140 --> 17:40.560
How so?

17:41.120 --> 17:42.920
The person executes perfectly,

17:43.280 --> 17:43.460
right?

17:43.840 --> 17:45.260
They are a perfectly virtuous,

17:45.400 --> 17:46.000
hardworking,

17:46.200 --> 17:47.260
uncomplaining instrument.

17:47.260 --> 17:49.260
But the authority over

17:49.260 --> 17:50.240
what that hard work

17:50.240 --> 17:51.180
actually achieves

17:51.180 --> 17:53.060
resides entirely elsewhere.

17:53.840 --> 17:55.200
They retain all the physical

17:55.200 --> 17:56.260
and mental capacities

17:56.260 --> 17:57.220
needed to execute,

17:57.760 --> 17:59.020
but zero authority

17:59.020 --> 17:59.780
over the direction.

18:00.580 --> 18:01.440
So it's like being

18:01.440 --> 18:03.260
the ultimate reverse centaur,

18:03.480 --> 18:04.540
but instead of a warehouse

18:04.540 --> 18:05.880
headset barking orders,

18:06.560 --> 18:07.600
the controller is your own

18:07.600 --> 18:09.260
internalized moral ideal

18:09.260 --> 18:09.880
that says,

18:10.440 --> 18:11.900
a good, virtuous person

18:11.900 --> 18:12.860
puts their head down

18:12.860 --> 18:13.520
and works hard

18:13.520 --> 18:14.240
without complaining.

18:14.780 --> 18:15.680
The virtue itself

18:15.680 --> 18:16.540
is the leash.

18:16.540 --> 18:19.160
The language of morality

18:19.160 --> 18:20.820
masks the structural reality

18:20.820 --> 18:22.180
that you have become

18:22.180 --> 18:22.900
an actuator.

18:23.520 --> 18:24.320
You don't feel like

18:24.320 --> 18:25.220
a slave to a machine.

18:25.540 --> 18:26.620
You feel like you are

18:26.620 --> 18:27.760
fulfilling a noble virtue.

18:28.280 --> 18:30.020
That is the Nietzschean trap.

18:30.480 --> 18:31.800
Okay, if we are getting

18:31.800 --> 18:33.000
captured by these purposes

18:33.000 --> 18:34.380
through our own virtues,

18:34.380 --> 18:35.300
we need to look at

18:35.300 --> 18:35.900
how a purpose

18:35.900 --> 18:37.180
actually gets locked in.

18:37.540 --> 18:38.300
Like, how do we,

18:38.520 --> 18:39.280
structurally speaking,

18:39.400 --> 18:40.180
commit to a purpose?

18:40.700 --> 18:42.000
The paper outlines

18:42.000 --> 18:42.940
something called

18:42.940 --> 18:44.400
the grammar of commitment.

18:44.400 --> 18:46.280
It's a five-step process,

18:46.400 --> 18:46.580
right?

18:46.820 --> 18:47.000
Yes.

18:47.360 --> 18:48.220
Palaytian argues

18:48.220 --> 18:48.740
that commitment

18:48.740 --> 18:49.380
to a purpose

18:49.380 --> 18:50.340
isn't just one

18:50.340 --> 18:51.100
spontaneous,

18:51.500 --> 18:52.320
monolithic choice.

18:52.420 --> 18:53.240
It's not a light switch.

18:53.860 --> 18:54.960
It proceeds through

18:54.960 --> 18:56.140
a sequence of five

18:56.140 --> 18:57.620
distinct operations.

18:57.900 --> 18:58.940
Let's trace these steps

18:58.940 --> 19:00.260
using a real-world example.

19:00.480 --> 19:00.960
Let's imagine

19:00.960 --> 19:01.820
a city council

19:01.820 --> 19:02.720
deciding to build

19:02.720 --> 19:04.080
a new public transit system.

19:04.520 --> 19:05.480
What is step one?

19:05.880 --> 19:06.800
The first operation

19:06.800 --> 19:07.980
is distinguish.

19:08.760 --> 19:09.360
This is simply

19:09.360 --> 19:10.120
the act of making

19:10.120 --> 19:11.180
a proposed purpose

19:11.180 --> 19:11.800
available

19:11.800 --> 19:12.840
as a candidate

19:12.840 --> 19:13.440
for action.

19:14.240 --> 19:15.020
Someone stands up

19:15.020 --> 19:15.660
at the council meeting

19:15.660 --> 19:16.020
and says,

19:16.620 --> 19:16.960
we could build

19:16.960 --> 19:17.840
a light rail system

19:17.840 --> 19:18.820
to connect the suburbs

19:18.820 --> 19:19.520
to downtown.

19:20.280 --> 19:21.000
You have distinguished

19:21.000 --> 19:21.960
a possibility

19:21.960 --> 19:23.040
from the void.

19:23.620 --> 19:23.840
Okay.

19:24.100 --> 19:25.260
The idea is on the table.

19:25.720 --> 19:26.100
Step two?

19:26.460 --> 19:27.640
The second operation

19:27.640 --> 19:28.840
is refuse.

19:29.580 --> 19:30.340
This is a critical

19:30.340 --> 19:31.340
filtering stage.

19:31.620 --> 19:32.120
You have to remove

19:32.120 --> 19:33.040
candidates that fail

19:33.040 --> 19:33.800
to meet applicable

19:33.800 --> 19:35.060
constraints or obligations.

19:35.820 --> 19:37.080
So, the council says,

19:37.640 --> 19:38.160
we can't build

19:38.160 --> 19:38.680
the light rail

19:38.680 --> 19:39.860
using highly toxic

19:39.860 --> 19:40.800
materials that will

19:40.800 --> 19:41.520
poison the groundwater.

19:41.800 --> 19:42.780
And we can't seize

19:42.780 --> 19:43.400
people's homes

19:43.400 --> 19:44.340
without due process.

19:44.580 --> 19:45.520
You filter out

19:45.520 --> 19:46.100
the variations

19:46.100 --> 19:46.900
that violate

19:46.900 --> 19:47.560
your boundaries.

19:48.500 --> 19:49.260
So, we have the idea

19:49.260 --> 19:50.540
and we've removed

19:50.540 --> 19:51.420
the illegal

19:51.420 --> 19:52.580
or unethical versions

19:52.580 --> 19:52.900
of it.

19:53.200 --> 19:53.920
What is step three?

19:54.280 --> 19:55.340
The third operation

19:55.340 --> 19:56.380
is bind.

19:56.780 --> 19:57.280
This is where

19:57.280 --> 19:58.180
the abstract idea

19:58.180 --> 19:59.160
starts hitting reality.

19:59.900 --> 20:00.700
You take the

20:00.700 --> 20:01.580
surviving proposal

20:01.580 --> 20:03.140
and you relate it

20:03.140 --> 20:04.300
to specific agents,

20:04.680 --> 20:05.320
to resources,

20:05.520 --> 20:06.220
and to obligations.

20:06.920 --> 20:07.260
You say,

20:07.460 --> 20:08.340
the Department of

20:08.340 --> 20:08.720
Transportation

20:08.720 --> 20:09.280
will spend

20:09.280 --> 20:10.020
$500 million

20:10.020 --> 20:10.840
over the next

20:10.840 --> 20:11.340
10 years.

20:11.340 --> 20:12.360
under these

20:12.360 --> 20:13.420
specific oversight

20:13.420 --> 20:14.760
rules to achieve

20:14.760 --> 20:16.260
this light rail network.

20:16.660 --> 20:17.260
You are binding

20:17.260 --> 20:18.060
the purpose

20:18.060 --> 20:19.300
to the real world.

20:20.000 --> 20:20.640
Distinguish,

20:20.860 --> 20:21.360
refuse,

20:21.760 --> 20:22.080
bind.

20:22.560 --> 20:24.180
What is the fourth step?

20:24.700 --> 20:25.540
The fourth operation

20:25.540 --> 20:26.160
is verify.

20:26.880 --> 20:27.660
This is the ultimate

20:27.660 --> 20:28.660
test of legitimacy.

20:29.660 --> 20:30.560
Before you break ground,

20:30.760 --> 20:31.480
you have to check

20:31.480 --> 20:32.440
whether the commitment

20:32.440 --> 20:33.580
you've just structured

20:33.580 --> 20:34.920
is actually warranted.

20:35.260 --> 20:36.320
Did the city council

20:36.320 --> 20:37.000
follow the right

20:37.000 --> 20:37.920
authorization rules?

20:38.120 --> 20:38.660
Do they hold

20:38.660 --> 20:39.260
public hearings?

20:39.260 --> 20:40.520
Do they actually

20:40.520 --> 20:41.160
have the legal

20:41.160 --> 20:41.960
standing and the

20:41.960 --> 20:42.900
consent of the governed

20:42.900 --> 20:44.140
to spend this money

20:44.140 --> 20:44.780
in this way?

20:45.120 --> 20:45.920
You are verifying

20:45.920 --> 20:46.980
the authority

20:46.980 --> 20:48.160
behind the binding.

20:48.820 --> 20:49.480
And if it passes

20:49.480 --> 20:50.080
verification,

20:50.460 --> 20:51.460
we hit the final step?

20:51.860 --> 20:52.200
Yes.

20:52.360 --> 20:53.760
The fifth operation

20:53.760 --> 20:54.700
is collapse.

20:55.440 --> 20:56.320
This is the point

20:56.320 --> 20:56.900
of no return.

20:57.580 --> 20:58.700
You collapse the field

20:58.700 --> 20:59.880
of all other possibilities

20:59.880 --> 21:01.480
into one definitive

21:01.480 --> 21:02.040
continuation.

21:02.040 --> 21:03.880
You sign the contracts,

21:04.380 --> 21:04.940
the bulldozers

21:04.940 --> 21:05.500
start moving,

21:05.940 --> 21:06.740
and that choice

21:06.740 --> 21:08.140
enters the historical record.

21:08.800 --> 21:09.280
Distinguish,

21:09.500 --> 21:09.880
refuse,

21:10.320 --> 21:10.700
bind,

21:11.280 --> 21:11.620
verify,

21:12.360 --> 21:12.820
collapse.

21:13.040 --> 21:13.640
I mean,

21:13.680 --> 21:14.300
it seems like

21:14.300 --> 21:15.460
a very logical,

21:16.160 --> 21:17.160
safe flow.

21:17.700 --> 21:18.520
If we follow

21:18.520 --> 21:19.120
this grammar,

21:19.300 --> 21:20.600
how do we get trapped?

21:20.960 --> 21:21.540
The paper notes

21:21.540 --> 21:22.120
that failures

21:22.120 --> 21:22.900
can be located

21:22.900 --> 21:23.960
at specific stages

21:23.960 --> 21:24.700
in this grammar.

21:24.860 --> 21:25.260
For example,

21:25.780 --> 21:27.040
a premature collapse

21:27.040 --> 21:28.320
is when you sign

21:28.320 --> 21:28.920
the contracts

21:28.920 --> 21:29.940
and start the bulldozers

21:29.940 --> 21:31.120
before you've actually

21:31.120 --> 21:32.640
finished the verification phase.

21:33.680 --> 21:34.240
That sounds bad.

21:34.680 --> 21:35.440
It is.

21:36.400 --> 21:37.640
But the massive failure point,

21:37.700 --> 21:38.500
the one most relevant

21:38.500 --> 21:39.920
to creating a reverse centaur,

21:40.120 --> 21:41.340
is a profound error

21:41.340 --> 21:42.860
in the bind stage.

21:43.140 --> 21:43.800
The paper calls it

21:43.800 --> 21:45.660
binding beyond scope.

21:46.440 --> 21:47.800
Binding beyond scope.

21:48.260 --> 21:49.360
Let's break that down.

21:49.400 --> 21:50.140
What does that actually

21:50.140 --> 21:51.120
look like in practice?

21:51.760 --> 21:52.320
This happens

21:52.320 --> 21:52.960
when a purpose

21:52.960 --> 21:54.280
or a specific way

21:54.280 --> 21:55.080
of valuing things

21:55.080 --> 21:56.380
is attached to a domain

21:56.380 --> 21:57.040
of obligations

21:57.040 --> 21:57.860
that its original

21:57.860 --> 21:59.160
authorization never covered.

21:59.440 --> 22:00.420
Let's shift away

22:00.420 --> 22:01.100
from the city council

22:01.100 --> 22:02.060
and look at a hospital.

22:02.380 --> 22:02.660
Okay.

22:03.660 --> 22:05.180
Imagine a hospital administrator

22:05.180 --> 22:06.280
develops a highly

22:06.280 --> 22:06.980
effective metric

22:06.980 --> 22:07.540
for measuring

22:07.540 --> 22:08.160
the efficiency

22:08.160 --> 22:09.780
of the hospital's

22:09.780 --> 22:10.500
laundry service.

22:10.960 --> 22:11.520
It measures

22:11.520 --> 22:12.400
the turnaround time

22:12.400 --> 22:13.100
of clean sheets

22:13.100 --> 22:13.940
per dollar spent.

22:14.880 --> 22:15.680
For the laundry room,

22:15.740 --> 22:16.860
it's a perfectly verified

22:16.860 --> 22:17.640
useful metric.

22:18.160 --> 22:18.440
Okay.

22:18.440 --> 22:19.360
It's a good metric

22:19.360 --> 22:20.800
for washing sheets.

22:21.220 --> 22:21.540
But then,

22:22.140 --> 22:23.180
binding beyond scope

22:23.180 --> 22:24.000
happens when that

22:24.000 --> 22:24.840
same administrator

22:24.840 --> 22:25.780
takes that exact

22:25.780 --> 22:26.940
same efficiency metric,

22:27.360 --> 22:28.440
turnaround time per dollar,

22:28.660 --> 22:29.360
and applies it

22:29.360 --> 22:30.440
to evaluate the performance

22:30.440 --> 22:31.740
of the psychiatric

22:31.740 --> 22:32.720
nursing staff

22:32.720 --> 22:34.060
or the palliative

22:34.060 --> 22:34.760
care doctors.

22:35.140 --> 22:35.820
Oh, wow.

22:36.100 --> 22:36.760
They take a metric

22:36.760 --> 22:37.660
designed for linen

22:37.660 --> 22:39.040
and use it to measure

22:39.040 --> 22:39.740
human empathy.

22:40.200 --> 22:40.640
Exactly.

22:40.640 --> 22:41.640
The valuation

22:41.640 --> 22:42.980
expands its jurisdiction

22:42.980 --> 22:44.040
into a zone

22:44.040 --> 22:44.840
where it was never

22:44.840 --> 22:45.740
verified to belong.

22:46.320 --> 22:47.380
It has bound itself

22:47.380 --> 22:48.300
beyond its scope.

22:48.300 --> 22:50.160
Now, if rival purposes

22:50.160 --> 22:51.600
like a nurse

22:51.600 --> 22:52.580
wanting to sit

22:52.580 --> 22:53.340
and hold the hand

22:53.340 --> 22:54.120
of a dying patient

22:54.120 --> 22:54.660
for an hour

22:54.660 --> 22:56.420
are formally excluded

22:56.420 --> 22:57.600
simply because they

22:57.600 --> 22:58.500
failed to maximize

22:58.500 --> 22:59.520
the turnaround

22:59.520 --> 23:00.520
efficiency metric,

23:01.000 --> 23:01.960
then the hospital's

23:01.960 --> 23:03.480
entire refusal stage

23:03.480 --> 23:04.860
is operating under

23:04.860 --> 23:05.720
an illegitimate,

23:06.060 --> 23:07.020
unverified authority.

23:07.220 --> 23:08.360
The nurse is told

23:08.360 --> 23:09.260
they are failing

23:09.260 --> 23:09.880
at their job,

23:09.960 --> 23:10.680
not because they are

23:10.680 --> 23:11.280
a bad nurse,

23:11.360 --> 23:13.400
but because a laundry metric

23:13.400 --> 23:14.720
has hijacked the system.

23:15.240 --> 23:16.320
And the terrifying part

23:16.320 --> 23:17.560
is that the collapse stage,

23:17.560 --> 23:18.860
the actual daily work

23:18.860 --> 23:19.900
being done in the hospital,

23:20.360 --> 23:21.180
might look highly

23:21.180 --> 23:22.020
efficient on paper.

23:22.600 --> 23:23.280
The beds are turned

23:23.280 --> 23:23.880
over fast,

23:24.320 --> 23:26.080
but the entire operation

23:26.080 --> 23:27.220
remains completely

23:27.220 --> 23:28.200
inadmissible

23:28.200 --> 23:29.640
because the foundation

23:29.640 --> 23:30.440
is flawed.

23:31.040 --> 23:32.060
That is exactly it.

23:32.560 --> 23:33.680
And this is the formal,

23:33.880 --> 23:34.660
structural counterpart

23:34.660 --> 23:35.560
to Nietzsche's warning.

23:36.180 --> 23:37.460
The means of preserving

23:37.460 --> 23:38.600
one very specific

23:38.600 --> 23:39.340
kind of life

23:39.340 --> 23:40.220
or organization,

23:40.760 --> 23:41.680
like an efficient

23:41.680 --> 23:42.440
laundry room,

23:42.920 --> 23:44.140
becomes a universal,

23:44.400 --> 23:45.360
tyrannical standard

23:45.360 --> 23:46.520
imposed on every

23:46.520 --> 23:47.540
other kind of life.

23:47.560 --> 23:48.320
But I want to play

23:48.320 --> 23:49.280
devil's advocate here

23:49.280 --> 23:49.800
for a second.

23:49.900 --> 23:50.240
Go for it.

23:50.360 --> 23:51.180
Because we are talking

23:51.180 --> 23:52.080
about delegation

23:52.080 --> 23:53.440
and automatic behavior

23:53.440 --> 23:54.180
as if they are

23:54.180 --> 23:55.400
inherently dangerous.

23:56.020 --> 23:57.300
But isn't delegation

23:57.300 --> 24:00.280
strictly neurologically necessary?

24:00.620 --> 24:00.840
I mean,

24:00.920 --> 24:02.480
we relegate complex tasks

24:02.480 --> 24:03.400
to automatic habit

24:03.400 --> 24:03.840
all the time.

24:04.140 --> 24:05.040
Think about when you first

24:05.040 --> 24:05.860
learned to drive a car.

24:06.220 --> 24:07.600
You were hyper aware

24:07.600 --> 24:08.680
of every single mirror,

24:08.940 --> 24:10.120
the pressure on the gas pedal,

24:10.200 --> 24:11.380
the angle of the steering wheel.

24:11.460 --> 24:12.560
You were explicitly

24:12.560 --> 24:13.760
deliberating every

24:13.760 --> 24:14.780
micro movement.

24:14.900 --> 24:15.880
It was exhausting.

24:16.160 --> 24:16.960
Oh yeah, terrifying.

24:16.960 --> 24:18.320
But after 10 years,

24:18.640 --> 24:19.740
you drive 30 miles

24:19.740 --> 24:21.400
to work on absolute autopilot.

24:21.540 --> 24:22.780
You aren't authorizing

24:22.780 --> 24:23.640
every single turn

24:23.640 --> 24:24.080
of the wheel.

24:24.300 --> 24:25.860
You are just executing.

24:26.280 --> 24:27.480
That kind of automatic

24:27.480 --> 24:29.040
delegation is a good thing,

24:29.080 --> 24:29.500
isn't it?

24:30.040 --> 24:32.260
Floxian entirely agrees

24:32.260 --> 24:32.600
with you

24:32.600 --> 24:33.740
and addresses this

24:33.740 --> 24:35.100
explicitly using a framework

24:35.100 --> 24:37.160
called aspect relegation theory.

24:38.000 --> 24:38.920
Moving explicit

24:38.920 --> 24:40.160
conscious deliberation

24:40.160 --> 24:42.020
into automatic relegated skill

24:42.020 --> 24:43.600
is absolutely necessary.

24:44.020 --> 24:44.820
It is an efficiency,

24:44.820 --> 24:46.260
not a lapse in morality.

24:47.340 --> 24:48.860
The fact that successful repetition

24:48.860 --> 24:50.380
allows you to move execution

24:50.380 --> 24:51.440
into automatic control

24:51.440 --> 24:52.580
is a feature

24:52.580 --> 24:53.740
of human cognition,

24:54.060 --> 24:54.620
not a bug.

24:55.300 --> 24:56.240
Okay, so if driving

24:56.240 --> 24:57.840
on autopilot is fine,

24:58.120 --> 24:59.760
where is the structural trap?

25:00.380 --> 25:01.580
The problem is never

25:01.580 --> 25:03.360
the automatic execution itself.

25:04.020 --> 25:05.240
The problem is the assumption

25:05.240 --> 25:07.140
that flawless automatic execution

25:07.140 --> 25:08.720
somehow retroactively

25:08.720 --> 25:10.180
handles the authorization.

25:10.180 --> 25:12.580
The paper formalizes this

25:12.580 --> 25:13.380
in its very first

25:13.380 --> 25:14.280
mathematical proof,

25:14.460 --> 25:15.040
Theorem 1,

25:15.420 --> 25:16.020
the independence

25:16.020 --> 25:16.860
of execution

25:16.860 --> 25:17.760
and authorization.

25:18.140 --> 25:18.820
I love this part.

25:19.180 --> 25:20.620
Let's walk through Theorem 1.

25:21.000 --> 25:21.980
How does the math

25:21.980 --> 25:22.920
actually prove

25:22.920 --> 25:23.620
that execution

25:23.620 --> 25:24.360
and authorization

25:24.360 --> 25:25.140
are independent?

25:25.800 --> 25:26.960
The theorem asks us

25:26.960 --> 25:27.500
to imagine

25:27.500 --> 25:28.840
a mathematical model

25:28.840 --> 25:29.660
with two different

25:29.660 --> 25:30.400
states of the world.

25:30.880 --> 25:31.500
Let's use your

25:31.500 --> 25:32.460
house building example.

25:32.880 --> 25:33.200
Perfect.

25:33.660 --> 25:34.340
In State 1,

25:34.740 --> 25:35.620
a master carpenter

25:35.620 --> 25:36.540
pursues the purpose

25:36.540 --> 25:37.440
of building a house,

25:37.440 --> 25:38.660
and they have

25:38.660 --> 25:39.240
the legitimate

25:39.240 --> 25:40.180
authorized standing

25:40.180 --> 25:40.780
to do so.

25:41.160 --> 25:42.180
The client hired them,

25:42.540 --> 25:43.440
the permits are signed.

25:44.220 --> 25:45.360
The authorization record

25:45.360 --> 25:46.340
for State 1 says

25:46.340 --> 25:47.700
1 for true.

25:48.740 --> 25:49.420
Okay, State 1

25:49.420 --> 25:51.020
is fully authorized 1.

25:51.380 --> 25:52.960
Now, in State 2,

25:53.480 --> 25:54.780
that exact same carpenter

25:54.780 --> 25:56.400
pursues the exact same purpose

25:56.400 --> 25:57.420
of building the house,

25:57.980 --> 25:58.980
but they have absolutely

25:58.980 --> 26:00.460
no authorization to do so.

26:01.060 --> 26:02.240
They just drove onto

26:02.240 --> 26:03.380
a stranger's empty lot

26:03.380 --> 26:04.060
and started building.

26:04.840 --> 26:06.140
The authorization record

26:06.140 --> 26:07.080
for State 2 says

26:07.080 --> 26:08.760
0 for false.

26:09.460 --> 26:09.960
Two states,

26:10.460 --> 26:11.240
one authorized,

26:11.460 --> 26:12.140
one trespassing.

26:12.620 --> 26:13.840
Now, here is the key.

26:14.720 --> 26:15.660
In both states,

26:16.140 --> 26:17.220
the carpenter executes

26:17.220 --> 26:18.580
the task flawlessly.

26:19.260 --> 26:20.640
The physical execution record,

26:21.360 --> 26:22.500
the speed of the hammering,

26:22.580 --> 26:23.620
the accuracy of the cuts,

26:23.860 --> 26:24.720
the physical movements

26:24.720 --> 26:25.280
of the worker,

26:25.680 --> 26:26.660
it is completely

26:26.660 --> 26:28.000
mathematically identical

26:28.000 --> 26:28.920
in both State 1

26:28.920 --> 26:29.780
and State 2.

26:30.240 --> 26:31.260
The house looks

26:31.260 --> 26:32.220
exactly the same.

26:32.620 --> 26:33.600
The joints are perfect

26:33.600 --> 26:34.520
in both scenarios.

26:34.940 --> 26:35.280
Exactly.

26:35.740 --> 26:35.960
Now,

26:35.960 --> 26:37.160
if you try to create

26:37.160 --> 26:38.240
a mathematical function,

26:38.640 --> 26:39.260
a predicate,

26:39.620 --> 26:40.700
that only looks

26:40.700 --> 26:42.080
at the execution record,

26:42.340 --> 26:43.500
it is going to output

26:43.500 --> 26:44.580
the exact same value

26:44.580 --> 26:45.280
in both states.

26:46.120 --> 26:47.280
Because the execution

26:47.280 --> 26:48.160
date is identical,

26:48.700 --> 26:49.640
the function will say,

26:50.140 --> 26:51.660
execution is perfect.

26:52.340 --> 26:53.180
The inspector looks

26:53.180 --> 26:54.060
at the joints and says,

26:54.140 --> 26:54.260
yep,

26:54.340 --> 26:55.380
100% execution.

26:55.380 --> 26:57.180
But the true authorization

26:57.180 --> 26:58.600
status is a 1

26:58.600 --> 26:59.340
in the first state

26:59.340 --> 27:01.020
and is 0 in the second.

27:02.380 --> 27:03.500
A single output value

27:03.500 --> 27:04.100
derived solely

27:04.100 --> 27:05.200
from the execution record

27:05.200 --> 27:06.360
cannot possibly equal

27:06.360 --> 27:09.060
both 1 and 0 simultaneously.

27:09.940 --> 27:10.280
Therefore,

27:11.360 --> 27:12.320
the theorem mathematically

27:12.320 --> 27:13.500
proves that no amount

27:13.500 --> 27:14.420
of execution data,

27:14.720 --> 27:15.580
no matter how flawless,

27:16.040 --> 27:16.920
no matter how efficient,

27:17.580 --> 27:18.860
can ever retroactively

27:18.860 --> 27:20.000
determine if the authorization

27:20.000 --> 27:21.820
was valid in the first place.

27:21.820 --> 27:24.420
Execution cannot determine

27:24.420 --> 27:25.080
authorization.

27:25.760 --> 27:27.220
You can't just point

27:27.220 --> 27:27.960
to how smoothly

27:27.960 --> 27:28.820
a system is running

27:28.820 --> 27:29.100
and say,

27:29.340 --> 27:29.540
see,

27:29.680 --> 27:30.280
it's fine.

27:30.820 --> 27:31.860
The fact that you are

27:31.860 --> 27:32.940
a highly efficient,

27:33.100 --> 27:34.180
perfectly greased gear

27:34.180 --> 27:34.880
in the machine

27:34.880 --> 27:35.860
does not prove

27:35.860 --> 27:36.380
that the machine

27:36.380 --> 27:37.860
actually belongs there.

27:37.860 --> 27:40.620
And this mathematical reality

27:40.620 --> 27:41.420
is exactly how

27:41.420 --> 27:42.680
the reverse centaur transition

27:42.680 --> 27:43.560
sneaks up on us.

27:44.400 --> 27:45.600
Success at a relegated,

27:45.960 --> 27:47.020
automatic task

27:47.020 --> 27:48.560
is used as an excuse

27:48.560 --> 27:49.360
by the system

27:49.360 --> 27:51.100
and by ourselves

27:51.100 --> 27:52.740
to stop examining

27:52.740 --> 27:54.120
the ends of that task.

27:55.260 --> 27:56.960
Authority slips away quietly

27:56.960 --> 27:58.340
through convenience,

27:58.840 --> 28:00.020
through accumulated dependence,

28:00.580 --> 28:01.700
and simply because

28:01.700 --> 28:03.140
it becomes too cognitively

28:03.140 --> 28:04.380
or politically costly

28:04.380 --> 28:06.280
to return to explicit judgment.

28:06.280 --> 28:07.960
We just keep driving the car

28:07.960 --> 28:09.260
because we are so good

28:09.260 --> 28:09.760
at driving

28:09.760 --> 28:11.040
and we forget to ask

28:11.040 --> 28:11.860
if we want to go

28:11.860 --> 28:12.760
to the destination.

28:13.560 --> 28:13.800
So,

28:14.440 --> 28:15.860
if we want to delegate safely,

28:16.080 --> 28:17.700
if we want to use habits

28:17.700 --> 28:18.420
and algorithms

28:18.420 --> 28:20.020
without being captured by them,

28:20.360 --> 28:21.320
what is the rule?

28:21.760 --> 28:23.080
We can't just hand off a task

28:23.080 --> 28:23.960
and walk away forever.

28:24.440 --> 28:25.780
Flyaction concludes this section

28:25.780 --> 28:26.480
by stating that

28:26.480 --> 28:27.720
an admissible delegation

28:27.720 --> 28:29.620
must have strictly defined

28:29.620 --> 28:30.780
return conditions.

28:31.280 --> 28:32.580
When you relegate a task

28:32.580 --> 28:33.760
to automatic execution,

28:34.160 --> 28:34.900
you have to specify

28:34.900 --> 28:37.040
exactly when that automatic execution

28:37.040 --> 28:37.780
must stop

28:37.780 --> 28:39.640
and explicit human judgment

28:39.640 --> 28:40.780
must reactivate.

28:40.980 --> 28:41.720
Give me an example

28:41.720 --> 28:42.680
of a return condition.

28:43.240 --> 28:44.040
A return condition

28:44.040 --> 28:45.380
is a tripwire.

28:45.880 --> 28:46.860
It could be triggered

28:46.860 --> 28:48.120
when underlying assumptions

28:48.120 --> 28:49.180
change in the environment.

28:49.760 --> 28:50.480
It could be triggered

28:50.480 --> 28:52.160
when two fundamental obligations

28:52.160 --> 28:53.020
suddenly conflict

28:53.020 --> 28:53.600
with each other.

28:53.980 --> 28:55.020
Or it could be triggered

28:55.020 --> 28:55.680
when the controller

28:55.680 --> 28:56.540
starts exceeding

28:56.540 --> 28:57.400
its original scope,

28:57.480 --> 28:59.020
like the hospital administrator

28:59.020 --> 29:00.540
trying to use laundry metrics

29:00.540 --> 29:01.340
on the nursing staff.

29:01.900 --> 29:02.940
When that happens,

29:02.940 --> 29:04.860
the system must force a return

29:04.860 --> 29:05.620
to explicit,

29:06.020 --> 29:07.040
conscious authorization.

29:07.540 --> 29:08.680
That makes perfect sense.

29:08.960 --> 29:09.980
But I can hear people

29:09.980 --> 29:10.740
listening to this

29:10.740 --> 29:11.220
and saying,

29:11.520 --> 29:12.000
okay, sure,

29:12.600 --> 29:14.020
execution doesn't prove authorization,

29:14.360 --> 29:15.380
but let's be real.

29:15.620 --> 29:16.520
What about the results?

29:16.920 --> 29:17.560
If a system,

29:17.740 --> 29:18.080
let's say,

29:18.440 --> 29:20.080
a sweeping economic policy

29:20.080 --> 29:21.280
or a corporate algorithm,

29:21.820 --> 29:22.900
generates massive,

29:23.200 --> 29:24.420
undeniable benefits,

29:24.520 --> 29:25.520
like record profits,

29:25.720 --> 29:26.580
higher crop yields,

29:26.720 --> 29:28.120
a massive increase in GDP,

29:28.780 --> 29:30.480
doesn't that high score

29:30.480 --> 29:32.660
essentially justify its existence?

29:33.140 --> 29:34.100
In our society,

29:34.200 --> 29:35.420
if it works and makes money,

29:35.600 --> 29:36.860
we usually give it a pass.

29:37.020 --> 29:37.600
We do, yeah.

29:37.920 --> 29:39.580
But the paper vehemently disagrees,

29:39.780 --> 29:40.400
which brings us

29:40.400 --> 29:42.080
to the core of optimization

29:42.080 --> 29:44.460
and the danger of the scoreboard.

29:44.620 --> 29:45.800
This takes us into theorems

29:45.800 --> 29:46.660
two and three,

29:47.020 --> 29:47.820
which deal directly

29:47.820 --> 29:48.920
with benefit optimization.

29:49.780 --> 29:51.280
And you hit the nail on the head.

29:51.400 --> 29:51.860
In our culture,

29:51.940 --> 29:53.980
a high score is often treated

29:53.980 --> 29:55.540
as the ultimate permission slip.

29:55.740 --> 29:57.100
If you maximize the benefit,

29:57.500 --> 29:58.680
you are considered untouchable.

29:58.800 --> 29:59.340
You are the winner.

29:59.340 --> 30:01.080
It makes me think of a dynamic

30:01.080 --> 30:02.740
you see in complex video games,

30:02.900 --> 30:05.040
particularly in speedrunning communities.

30:05.220 --> 30:05.500
Oh, yeah.

30:06.200 --> 30:07.780
Imagine you are playing a game

30:07.780 --> 30:09.620
and your ultimate stated goal

30:09.620 --> 30:10.660
is to maximize your score

30:10.660 --> 30:11.480
as fast as possible.

30:11.820 --> 30:12.940
You play for a while

30:12.940 --> 30:14.560
and then you discover a glitch

30:14.560 --> 30:15.920
in the game's underlying code.

30:16.520 --> 30:18.340
Maybe if you wedge your character

30:18.340 --> 30:20.380
against a specific corner of a wall

30:20.380 --> 30:21.460
and jump repeatedly,

30:21.960 --> 30:23.220
the physics engine breaks

30:23.220 --> 30:25.460
and your score just ticks up to infinity,

30:26.180 --> 30:27.420
you have maximized your score

30:27.420 --> 30:29.060
faster and more efficiently

30:29.060 --> 30:30.020
than anyone else

30:30.020 --> 30:31.040
who is playing the game normally.

30:31.540 --> 30:33.420
You are at the top of the leaderboard,

30:33.640 --> 30:34.940
but you got there

30:34.940 --> 30:36.080
by exploiting a glitch

30:36.080 --> 30:37.720
that breaks the actual rules

30:37.720 --> 30:38.580
of the game universe.

30:39.280 --> 30:40.380
Your high score doesn't mean

30:40.380 --> 30:41.520
you are the most skilled player.

30:41.960 --> 30:43.240
It just means you stepped outside

30:43.240 --> 30:44.640
the legitimate bounds of the game

30:44.640 --> 30:45.780
to manipulate the output.

30:46.040 --> 30:47.960
That is a phenomenal analogy

30:47.960 --> 30:49.240
for what theorem two

30:49.240 --> 30:50.320
is mathematically proving.

30:51.380 --> 30:52.900
Theorem two is explicitly titled

30:52.900 --> 30:55.160
benefit maximization is insufficient.

30:55.160 --> 30:57.640
It proves that just because

30:57.640 --> 30:58.980
an action maximizes

30:58.980 --> 31:00.180
an estimated benefit,

31:00.600 --> 31:02.420
that fact alone does not make

31:02.420 --> 31:03.640
the action what the paper

31:03.640 --> 31:04.700
calls admissible.

31:05.540 --> 31:06.020
Admissible.

31:06.340 --> 31:07.940
We've used that word a few times.

31:08.220 --> 31:09.960
What exactly does admissibility

31:09.960 --> 31:11.500
mean in this structural context?

31:11.960 --> 31:13.860
Admissibility is a comprehensive check

31:13.860 --> 31:15.240
on the entire provenance

31:15.240 --> 31:15.760
of an action.

31:16.360 --> 31:17.240
It doesn't just look

31:17.240 --> 31:17.880
at the final score.

31:18.680 --> 31:19.900
It asks a series

31:19.900 --> 31:21.240
of structural questions.

31:22.000 --> 31:23.380
Are the initial objectives

31:23.380 --> 31:24.280
actually valid?

31:25.280 --> 31:25.940
Are the estimates

31:25.940 --> 31:26.940
of the benefits fair

31:26.940 --> 31:27.700
and unbiased?

31:28.400 --> 31:29.840
Were any required

31:29.840 --> 31:31.020
hidden costs

31:31.020 --> 31:32.820
externalized onto someone else?

31:33.520 --> 31:34.280
And most importantly,

31:34.500 --> 31:36.040
does this action violate

31:36.040 --> 31:36.900
any applicable

31:36.900 --> 31:38.520
fundamental obligations?

31:39.140 --> 31:40.580
Like the fundamental

31:40.580 --> 31:41.660
side constraints

31:41.660 --> 31:42.260
on the game.

31:42.340 --> 31:42.920
You can't break

31:42.920 --> 31:44.300
the physics engine to win.

31:44.620 --> 31:44.900
Yes.

31:45.820 --> 31:46.720
Theorem two sets up

31:46.720 --> 31:48.840
a very clear mathematical scenario

31:48.840 --> 31:49.560
to prove this.

31:50.360 --> 31:52.360
Imagine you are an organization

31:52.360 --> 31:54.180
faced with two possible actions.

31:54.820 --> 31:55.260
Action A

31:55.260 --> 31:56.280
and Action B.

31:56.900 --> 31:57.820
You run the projections.

31:58.820 --> 31:59.420
Action A

31:59.420 --> 32:00.720
generates a massive,

32:01.180 --> 32:02.740
towering benefit score.

32:03.420 --> 32:04.180
It is the clear,

32:04.620 --> 32:05.580
unambiguous winner

32:05.580 --> 32:06.320
on the scoreboard.

32:07.180 --> 32:07.900
Action B

32:07.900 --> 32:08.980
generates a much,

32:09.060 --> 32:09.940
much lower score.

32:10.500 --> 32:11.380
It looks inefficient

32:11.380 --> 32:12.080
by comparison.

32:12.780 --> 32:13.140
However,

32:13.640 --> 32:14.820
there is an applicable

32:14.820 --> 32:15.540
obligation,

32:16.180 --> 32:16.740
a fundamental,

32:16.960 --> 32:17.200
ethical,

32:17.200 --> 32:18.520
or legal rule

32:18.520 --> 32:19.960
that says a specific

32:19.960 --> 32:21.840
condition must be met

32:21.840 --> 32:22.400
for an action

32:22.400 --> 32:23.180
to be admissible.

32:24.140 --> 32:24.840
Action B

32:24.840 --> 32:26.600
meets this fundamental condition.

32:27.540 --> 32:28.200
Action A,

32:28.520 --> 32:29.020
in its pursuit

32:29.020 --> 32:29.800
of the high score,

32:30.400 --> 32:31.020
violates it.

32:31.840 --> 32:32.480
So Action A

32:32.480 --> 32:33.300
breaks the rule

32:33.300 --> 32:34.420
but gets all the points.

32:34.700 --> 32:35.060
Exactly.

32:35.880 --> 32:36.740
The theorem proves

32:36.740 --> 32:37.840
that because Action A

32:37.840 --> 32:39.520
violates a necessary condition,

32:40.240 --> 32:41.700
its admissibility value

32:41.700 --> 32:43.200
is mathematically zero.

32:43.920 --> 32:44.600
It does not matter

32:44.600 --> 32:45.860
if its estimated benefit score

32:45.860 --> 32:46.840
is a million times

32:46.840 --> 32:47.780
higher than Action B.

32:48.580 --> 32:49.860
The unique maximizer

32:49.860 --> 32:51.020
of the estimated benefit

32:51.020 --> 32:53.040
is completely inadmissible.

32:53.560 --> 32:54.540
So a high score cannot,

32:54.860 --> 32:56.740
under any mathematical circumstance,

32:57.180 --> 32:59.000
override a fundamental obligation.

32:59.340 --> 32:59.560
Right.

32:59.880 --> 33:01.840
And to ground this in philosophy,

33:02.380 --> 33:03.460
the paper mentions thinkers

33:03.460 --> 33:04.300
like John Rawls

33:04.300 --> 33:05.080
and Robert Nozick.

33:05.600 --> 33:06.680
They championed

33:06.680 --> 33:07.720
this exact concept,

33:08.180 --> 33:09.320
often referred to as

33:09.320 --> 33:10.560
side constraints

33:10.560 --> 33:12.440
or the separateness

33:12.440 --> 33:13.240
of persons.

33:13.880 --> 33:14.860
The core idea

33:14.860 --> 33:16.080
is that fundamental

33:16.080 --> 33:17.060
ethical obligations

33:17.060 --> 33:18.660
like basic human rights

33:18.660 --> 33:20.060
or individual dignity

33:20.060 --> 33:21.780
or strict legal boundaries

33:21.780 --> 33:23.280
act as hard,

33:23.740 --> 33:24.940
impassable walls

33:24.940 --> 33:26.160
that constrain

33:26.160 --> 33:26.980
the maximization

33:26.980 --> 33:27.640
of a good.

33:28.540 --> 33:29.260
They are not just

33:29.260 --> 33:30.180
another variable

33:30.180 --> 33:31.420
in the math equation

33:31.420 --> 33:32.780
that you can trade away

33:32.780 --> 33:33.440
to get a higher

33:33.440 --> 33:34.180
overall score.

33:34.440 --> 33:35.460
You can't say,

33:35.820 --> 33:36.560
well, yes,

33:36.680 --> 33:38.320
we violated the labor rights

33:38.320 --> 33:39.740
of 10 warehouse workers

33:39.740 --> 33:40.860
and they suffered terribly,

33:41.080 --> 33:42.520
but we increased

33:42.520 --> 33:43.260
shareholder value

33:43.260 --> 33:44.060
by 200%,

33:44.060 --> 33:44.660
so the math

33:44.660 --> 33:45.680
that's out in our favor.

33:45.920 --> 33:46.280
Exactly.

33:47.140 --> 33:48.020
The rights of the workers

33:48.020 --> 33:49.520
are a side constraint,

33:49.920 --> 33:50.980
not a tradable commodity.

33:51.600 --> 33:52.380
A system that just

33:52.380 --> 33:54.180
blindly optimizes a metric

33:54.180 --> 33:55.360
without acknowledging

33:55.360 --> 33:56.480
those side constraints

33:56.480 --> 33:57.720
has to answer

33:57.720 --> 33:59.940
a severe structural question.

34:00.640 --> 34:01.220
Who decided

34:01.220 --> 34:02.780
that this specific metric,

34:03.160 --> 34:04.480
like shareholder value

34:04.480 --> 34:05.680
or click-through rate,

34:05.980 --> 34:06.900
is the ultimate

34:06.900 --> 34:09.020
universally authoritative good?

34:09.340 --> 34:10.840
And whose hidden purposes

34:10.840 --> 34:12.500
suddenly became authoritative

34:12.500 --> 34:13.660
when that definition

34:13.660 --> 34:14.420
was accepted?

34:15.100 --> 34:15.700
It's the binding

34:15.700 --> 34:17.100
beyond scope error again,

34:17.260 --> 34:18.540
but on a massive

34:18.540 --> 34:19.520
societal scale.

34:19.920 --> 34:20.140
Yes.

34:20.580 --> 34:21.520
And I want to ensure

34:21.520 --> 34:22.280
we frame this

34:22.280 --> 34:23.860
carefully and impartially,

34:24.000 --> 34:25.100
just as the paper does.

34:25.520 --> 34:26.480
The text points out

34:26.480 --> 34:28.140
that this structural question

34:28.140 --> 34:29.680
applies universally

34:29.680 --> 34:31.320
across all ideologies.

34:31.740 --> 34:32.800
It applies to a rigid

34:32.800 --> 34:33.960
corporate profit metric.

34:34.580 --> 34:35.760
It applies to a sweeping

34:35.760 --> 34:37.360
government utilitarian program.

34:37.820 --> 34:39.460
It applies to a religious mission.

34:40.000 --> 34:41.420
The paper even explicitly

34:41.420 --> 34:43.020
references the effective

34:43.020 --> 34:44.080
altruism movement

34:44.080 --> 34:45.980
as a scholarly application

34:45.980 --> 34:46.680
of this problem.

34:47.340 --> 34:47.360
Right.

34:47.480 --> 34:49.200
And just to be absolutely clear

34:49.200 --> 34:49.960
for you listening,

34:50.200 --> 34:51.680
we are looking at this structurally.

34:51.920 --> 34:53.380
We are not taking a political

34:53.380 --> 34:54.380
or moral side

34:54.380 --> 34:55.160
on the effective

34:55.160 --> 34:56.860
altruism movement itself.

34:57.080 --> 34:58.300
The paper is simply

34:58.300 --> 35:00.160
emphasizing the structural reality

35:00.160 --> 35:02.060
that even highly altruistic,

35:02.260 --> 35:03.940
incredibly benevolent purposes,

35:04.440 --> 35:05.160
like trying to save

35:05.160 --> 35:06.160
the maximum number

35:06.160 --> 35:06.900
of human lives

35:06.900 --> 35:08.360
possible per dollar spent,

35:08.360 --> 35:10.180
must still be adopted

35:10.180 --> 35:11.880
through an admissible process.

35:12.660 --> 35:13.520
A benevolent purpose

35:13.520 --> 35:14.880
isn't magically exempt

35:14.880 --> 35:16.720
from needing legitimate authorization

35:16.720 --> 35:18.660
and respecting side constraints.

35:18.960 --> 35:20.280
That is precisely

35:20.280 --> 35:21.140
Flaxen's point.

35:21.680 --> 35:22.760
A benevolent purpose

35:22.760 --> 35:23.500
that is adopted

35:23.500 --> 35:25.000
through an admissible process

35:25.000 --> 35:26.380
is fantastic.

35:27.040 --> 35:28.580
But the sheer benevolence

35:28.580 --> 35:29.220
of the goal

35:29.220 --> 35:30.300
doesn't grant you

35:30.300 --> 35:30.920
a free pass

35:30.920 --> 35:31.920
to ignore authorization

35:31.920 --> 35:33.420
and steamroll

35:33.420 --> 35:35.000
over ethical side constraints.

35:35.560 --> 35:36.000
The ends

35:36.000 --> 35:37.420
do not retroactively

35:37.420 --> 35:38.480
authorize the means.

35:39.020 --> 35:40.060
Okay, I think

35:40.060 --> 35:41.480
we have solidly established

35:41.480 --> 35:42.560
that the highest score

35:42.560 --> 35:43.600
isn't necessarily

35:43.600 --> 35:44.760
the right action.

35:45.380 --> 35:46.300
But if that is true,

35:46.580 --> 35:48.020
why is it so incredibly easy

35:48.020 --> 35:49.000
for us to get fooled

35:49.000 --> 35:49.700
by the score?

35:50.280 --> 35:51.580
Why do entire corporations,

35:52.080 --> 35:52.400
governments,

35:52.800 --> 35:53.580
and individuals

35:53.580 --> 35:54.680
constantly stare

35:54.680 --> 35:55.540
at the scoreboard

35:55.540 --> 35:56.740
and completely forget

35:56.740 --> 35:57.820
to check the rules?

35:58.280 --> 35:58.880
That vulnerability

35:58.880 --> 36:00.380
brings us to theorem four,

36:00.860 --> 36:01.600
which deals with

36:01.600 --> 36:02.960
the representation criterion.

36:03.460 --> 36:04.960
It explains the mathematical,

36:05.340 --> 36:06.120
cognitive danger

36:06.120 --> 36:07.760
of relying on scalar numbers.

36:08.080 --> 36:09.140
A scalar number

36:09.140 --> 36:10.280
being just a single,

36:10.620 --> 36:11.720
one-dimensional quantity,

36:12.000 --> 36:13.360
like a profit margin

36:13.360 --> 36:15.020
or a body mass index

36:15.020 --> 36:16.240
or a GDP figure.

36:16.660 --> 36:17.020
Yes.

36:17.540 --> 36:19.040
As humans trying to navigate

36:19.040 --> 36:20.620
a wildly complex world,

36:20.720 --> 36:21.820
we rely on representations

36:21.820 --> 36:24.360
to compress complex realities

36:24.360 --> 36:24.940
into something

36:24.940 --> 36:26.100
our brains can manage.

36:26.820 --> 36:27.580
A benefit score

36:27.580 --> 36:28.360
is a representation

36:28.360 --> 36:29.780
of an action's value.

36:29.780 --> 36:31.760
But theorem four

36:31.760 --> 36:33.500
asks a very strict question.

36:34.140 --> 36:35.740
Under what mathematical conditions

36:35.740 --> 36:36.960
does a representation

36:36.960 --> 36:38.220
actually preserve

36:38.220 --> 36:39.180
the admissibility

36:39.180 --> 36:39.740
of the thing

36:39.740 --> 36:40.560
it is measuring?

36:41.400 --> 36:42.060
When can we actually

36:42.060 --> 36:42.860
trust the score

36:42.860 --> 36:43.740
to tell us the truth

36:43.740 --> 36:44.680
about whether an action

36:44.680 --> 36:45.280
was allowed?

36:45.740 --> 36:46.660
The proof shows

36:46.660 --> 36:47.200
that a function

36:47.200 --> 36:47.780
of the score

36:47.780 --> 36:49.180
can only truly represent

36:49.180 --> 36:49.880
admissibility

36:49.880 --> 36:50.840
if admissibility

36:50.840 --> 36:51.780
is constant

36:51.780 --> 36:53.340
across all actions

36:53.340 --> 36:54.500
that get the same score.

36:55.080 --> 36:56.060
The mathematical term

36:56.060 --> 36:56.460
for this

36:56.460 --> 36:57.920
is being constant

36:57.920 --> 36:58.900
on its fibers.

36:59.740 --> 36:59.980
Okay.

37:00.280 --> 37:02.240
Constant on its fibers.

37:02.700 --> 37:03.520
That sounds like

37:03.520 --> 37:04.240
advanced geometry.

37:04.480 --> 37:05.320
Let's ground that.

37:05.400 --> 37:05.880
Walk me through

37:05.880 --> 37:06.760
exactly what that means.

37:07.180 --> 37:07.860
Let's use a very

37:07.860 --> 37:08.840
concrete example.

37:09.280 --> 37:10.360
Imagine two completely

37:10.360 --> 37:11.620
different corporate actions

37:11.620 --> 37:12.900
that both result

37:12.900 --> 37:13.480
in generating

37:13.480 --> 37:14.720
exactly $10,000

37:14.720 --> 37:15.420
in profit.

37:16.180 --> 37:16.940
The representation

37:16.940 --> 37:17.940
of both actions,

37:18.300 --> 37:18.960
their score

37:18.960 --> 37:19.560
on the spreadsheet,

37:20.000 --> 37:20.680
is identical,

37:21.180 --> 37:22.460
a positive $10,000.

37:22.460 --> 37:24.580
Now, suppose

37:24.580 --> 37:25.260
action one

37:25.260 --> 37:25.880
was achieved

37:25.880 --> 37:26.440
legitimately.

37:27.120 --> 37:28.060
The company innovated,

37:28.280 --> 37:28.880
they built a great

37:28.880 --> 37:29.340
new product,

37:29.460 --> 37:30.140
people loved it,

37:30.360 --> 37:31.380
and they made $10,000.

37:32.040 --> 37:32.600
Okay.

37:33.000 --> 37:33.440
Action one

37:33.440 --> 37:34.580
is clearly admissible.

37:35.040 --> 37:36.060
But action two

37:36.060 --> 37:36.600
was achieved

37:36.600 --> 37:38.060
by a factory manager

37:38.060 --> 37:39.600
deciding to illegally

37:39.600 --> 37:40.700
dump toxic waste

37:40.700 --> 37:41.660
into a local river

37:41.660 --> 37:42.440
in order to cut

37:42.440 --> 37:43.460
disposal costs.

37:44.100 --> 37:45.560
That cost-cutting measure

37:45.560 --> 37:46.720
saved the company

37:46.720 --> 37:47.820
exactly $10,000.

37:48.460 --> 37:48.880
Wow.

37:49.060 --> 37:49.300
Okay.

37:50.000 --> 37:50.740
So action two

37:50.740 --> 37:52.160
is wildly inadmissible.

37:52.460 --> 37:53.640
It violates basic

37:53.640 --> 37:54.740
legal and moral

37:54.740 --> 37:55.520
side constraints.

37:55.920 --> 37:56.640
But look at

37:56.640 --> 37:57.440
the scalar number.

37:58.060 --> 37:59.580
The $10,000 profit figure

37:59.580 --> 38:00.760
is completely

38:00.760 --> 38:02.100
mathematically identical

38:02.100 --> 38:02.920
for both actions.

38:03.460 --> 38:04.520
The representation

38:04.520 --> 38:05.420
has compressed

38:05.420 --> 38:06.020
the reality

38:06.020 --> 38:06.900
so severely

38:06.900 --> 38:08.680
that it has squashed

38:08.680 --> 38:10.140
and utterly destroyed

38:10.140 --> 38:11.060
the vital distinction

38:11.060 --> 38:11.900
between the

38:11.900 --> 38:12.880
authorized action

38:12.880 --> 38:14.320
and the horrific

38:14.320 --> 38:15.320
unauthorized one.

38:15.900 --> 38:16.800
Because an admissible

38:16.800 --> 38:17.860
action and an

38:17.860 --> 38:18.760
inadmissible action

38:18.760 --> 38:19.440
can both result

38:19.440 --> 38:20.620
in the exact same score,

38:21.360 --> 38:22.000
admissibility

38:22.000 --> 38:23.140
is not constant

38:23.140 --> 38:24.000
on the fiber

38:24.000 --> 38:24.520
of the score

38:24.520 --> 38:25.140
$10,000.

38:25.740 --> 38:26.300
Therefore,

38:26.500 --> 38:27.280
the score itself

38:27.280 --> 38:28.120
is structurally

38:28.120 --> 38:29.360
incapable of telling

38:29.360 --> 38:30.280
you if the action

38:30.280 --> 38:31.020
was admissible.

38:31.680 --> 38:32.660
You cannot look

38:32.660 --> 38:33.200
at a spreadsheet

38:33.200 --> 38:34.160
and know if you

38:34.160 --> 38:35.080
are doing the right thing.

38:35.520 --> 38:35.920
Exactly.

38:36.600 --> 38:37.300
The single number

38:37.300 --> 38:38.120
hides the history

38:38.120 --> 38:38.880
of how the number

38:38.880 --> 38:39.540
was achieved.

38:40.000 --> 38:40.460
The score

38:40.460 --> 38:42.100
squashes the context.

38:43.220 --> 38:44.520
An overly simple metric

38:44.520 --> 38:45.940
doesn't just measure reality.

38:46.340 --> 38:47.640
It acts as a camouflage

38:47.640 --> 38:49.160
for unauthorized purposes.

38:49.660 --> 38:50.380
That is chilling.

38:50.980 --> 38:52.580
We build our entire world

38:52.580 --> 38:53.580
around maximizing

38:53.580 --> 38:54.460
these squashed

38:54.460 --> 38:55.780
out-of-context metrics.

38:56.320 --> 38:57.180
So we know

38:57.180 --> 38:58.160
a high score

38:58.160 --> 38:58.680
can mask

38:58.680 --> 38:59.760
an unauthorized purpose.

39:00.240 --> 39:01.000
We know execution

39:01.000 --> 39:02.220
doesn't prove authorization.

39:02.900 --> 39:03.740
What happens

39:03.740 --> 39:04.700
when the illusion breaks?

39:05.380 --> 39:05.860
What happens

39:05.860 --> 39:06.400
when you finally

39:06.400 --> 39:07.020
look around,

39:07.500 --> 39:08.100
you realize

39:08.100 --> 39:08.600
the context

39:08.600 --> 39:09.420
has been squashed,

39:09.480 --> 39:09.980
and you realize

39:09.980 --> 39:11.580
you are a reverse centaur

39:11.580 --> 39:12.640
serving a metric

39:12.640 --> 39:13.440
you never chose?

39:13.920 --> 39:14.900
You want out.

39:14.900 --> 39:15.960
But what does

39:15.960 --> 39:16.780
trying to escape

39:16.780 --> 39:17.780
actually look like

39:17.780 --> 39:18.440
structurally?

39:19.140 --> 39:19.800
This takes us

39:19.800 --> 39:20.460
to the geometry

39:20.460 --> 39:21.100
of choices

39:21.100 --> 39:22.240
and the concept

39:22.240 --> 39:23.440
of corrective reachability

39:23.440 --> 39:24.820
and excluded cuts.

39:25.300 --> 39:26.140
To explain how we get

39:26.140 --> 39:27.080
physically, legally,

39:27.180 --> 39:28.720
or organizationally trapped,

39:29.380 --> 39:30.160
Flagson shifts

39:30.160 --> 39:30.820
the methodology

39:30.820 --> 39:32.160
from epistemology

39:32.160 --> 39:33.700
into graph theory.

39:34.440 --> 39:35.040
This is where

39:35.040 --> 39:36.040
we literally map out

39:36.040 --> 39:36.640
the geometry

39:36.640 --> 39:37.440
of the trap.

39:38.040 --> 39:38.620
We are looking

39:38.620 --> 39:39.160
at the layout

39:39.160 --> 39:39.860
of our choices

39:39.860 --> 39:40.720
as a network

39:40.720 --> 39:42.040
of nodes and pathways.

39:42.580 --> 39:43.140
I want to make sure

39:43.140 --> 39:44.240
I can visualize this.

39:44.240 --> 39:45.280
How should I picture

39:45.280 --> 39:45.820
this graph?

39:46.560 --> 39:48.520
Imagine a massive whiteboard.

39:49.060 --> 39:50.140
Every possible state

39:50.140 --> 39:51.160
of your organization

39:51.160 --> 39:52.700
or your career

39:52.700 --> 39:54.500
or your life

39:54.500 --> 39:55.860
is a single dot

39:55.860 --> 39:56.600
on that whiteboard.

39:57.020 --> 39:58.000
These dots are called

39:58.000 --> 39:59.760
vertices in graph theory.

40:00.420 --> 40:01.900
Now, draw lines

40:01.900 --> 40:03.380
connecting those dots

40:03.380 --> 40:04.600
wherever it is

40:04.600 --> 40:05.640
operationally

40:05.640 --> 40:06.840
or physically feasible

40:06.840 --> 40:07.560
to move from

40:07.560 --> 40:08.640
one state to another.

40:09.180 --> 40:10.740
This entire tangled

40:10.740 --> 40:11.700
web of lines

40:11.700 --> 40:12.080
is called

40:12.080 --> 40:13.620
the feasible graph.

40:13.620 --> 40:14.700
It represents

40:14.700 --> 40:15.760
everything you can

40:15.760 --> 40:16.540
physically do

40:16.540 --> 40:17.580
in the universe.

40:17.900 --> 40:19.360
Okay, so I am

40:19.360 --> 40:20.120
at the dot labeled

40:20.120 --> 40:20.880
current job.

40:21.180 --> 40:22.320
I can draw a line

40:22.320 --> 40:23.140
to the dot labeled

40:23.140 --> 40:24.080
stay at my job.

40:24.400 --> 40:25.260
I can draw a line

40:25.260 --> 40:26.460
to quit my job.

40:26.860 --> 40:28.040
I can also draw a line

40:28.040 --> 40:29.160
to steal all

40:29.160 --> 40:30.020
the office computers

40:30.020 --> 40:30.500
and sell them

40:30.500 --> 40:31.220
on the black market

40:31.220 --> 40:32.200
or set the building

40:32.200 --> 40:32.640
on fire.

40:32.900 --> 40:33.800
Those are all

40:33.800 --> 40:34.880
physically feasible

40:34.880 --> 40:35.920
moves I could make today.

40:36.440 --> 40:36.560
Right.

40:37.000 --> 40:38.000
But obviously

40:38.000 --> 40:39.400
you can't just do

40:39.400 --> 40:40.120
anything that is

40:40.120 --> 40:41.000
physically possible.

40:41.000 --> 40:42.340
the controller

40:42.340 --> 40:42.960
of the system

40:42.960 --> 40:43.920
your boss

40:43.920 --> 40:45.500
the software constraints

40:45.500 --> 40:46.140
of your computer

40:46.140 --> 40:47.200
the local police force

40:47.200 --> 40:48.540
they place limits

40:48.540 --> 40:48.920
on you.

40:49.480 --> 40:50.240
They take an eraser

40:50.240 --> 40:50.960
to the whiteboard

40:50.960 --> 40:51.580
and they erase

40:51.580 --> 40:52.780
a bunch of those lines.

40:53.220 --> 40:54.400
What is left over

40:54.400 --> 40:55.200
is called

40:55.200 --> 40:56.260
the permitted graph.

40:56.940 --> 40:57.700
These are the moves

40:57.700 --> 40:58.180
the controller

40:58.180 --> 40:59.200
actually allows you

40:59.200 --> 40:59.620
to make

40:59.620 --> 41:00.680
without triggering

41:00.680 --> 41:01.800
a massive penalty

41:01.800 --> 41:03.700
or physical intervention.

41:04.460 --> 41:05.240
Okay, so the path

41:05.240 --> 41:06.680
to steal all the computers

41:06.680 --> 41:07.920
is heavily erased.

41:08.140 --> 41:08.900
It's feasible

41:08.900 --> 41:09.980
but definitely

41:09.980 --> 41:10.660
not permitted.

41:11.120 --> 41:12.060
Then we have a third

41:12.060 --> 41:13.760
even more restricted graph.

41:14.200 --> 41:14.860
This is the

41:14.860 --> 41:16.600
obligation preserving graph.

41:17.280 --> 41:17.940
This takes

41:17.940 --> 41:18.820
the permitted graph

41:18.820 --> 41:20.180
and further erases

41:20.180 --> 41:21.120
any lines that

41:21.120 --> 41:22.020
while allowed

41:22.020 --> 41:22.820
by the controller

41:22.820 --> 41:24.080
would cause you

41:24.080 --> 41:24.500
to violate

41:24.500 --> 41:25.060
your own

41:25.060 --> 41:26.120
fundamental ethical

41:26.120 --> 41:26.640
legal

41:26.640 --> 41:28.260
or professional obligations.

41:29.000 --> 41:29.880
Ah, I see.

41:30.360 --> 41:31.320
So if I am

41:31.320 --> 41:32.160
a surgeon

41:32.160 --> 41:33.480
and I am in the middle

41:33.480 --> 41:34.700
of a complex operation

41:34.700 --> 41:36.120
the physical path

41:36.120 --> 41:37.100
to quit my job

41:37.100 --> 41:37.900
and walk out the door

41:37.900 --> 41:38.380
right now

41:38.380 --> 41:39.580
might be feasible

41:39.580 --> 41:41.040
and it might not be

41:41.040 --> 41:41.920
strictly illegal

41:41.920 --> 41:43.400
in a right-to-work state

41:43.400 --> 41:45.000
but it is erased

41:45.000 --> 41:45.840
from the obligation

41:45.840 --> 41:46.880
preserving graph

41:46.880 --> 41:48.280
because walking out

41:48.280 --> 41:48.680
would mean

41:48.680 --> 41:49.560
abandoning a patient

41:49.560 --> 41:50.440
and violating

41:50.440 --> 41:51.060
my fundamental

41:51.060 --> 41:51.960
medical oath.

41:52.340 --> 41:52.780
Exactly.

41:53.600 --> 41:54.380
So we have

41:54.380 --> 41:55.560
these nested layers

41:55.560 --> 41:56.240
of reality.

41:56.800 --> 41:58.100
What is physically feasible

41:58.100 --> 41:59.920
what the system permits

41:59.920 --> 42:01.160
and what actually

42:01.160 --> 42:02.420
preserves your obligations.

42:03.200 --> 42:04.020
Now for a system

42:04.020 --> 42:04.740
to be considered

42:04.740 --> 42:05.980
structurally legitimate

42:05.980 --> 42:07.400
it must preserve

42:07.400 --> 42:08.500
at least one pathway

42:08.500 --> 42:09.720
in that final graph

42:09.720 --> 42:10.860
that leads to

42:10.860 --> 42:11.860
what Flyxion calls

42:11.860 --> 42:12.900
a corrective state.

42:13.740 --> 42:14.620
A corrective state

42:14.620 --> 42:15.560
is a safe harbor.

42:16.220 --> 42:17.000
It is a place

42:17.000 --> 42:17.820
where you can revise

42:17.820 --> 42:18.620
contest

42:18.620 --> 42:19.480
or terminate

42:19.480 --> 42:20.280
a bad purpose

42:20.280 --> 42:21.840
while still successfully

42:21.840 --> 42:22.440
discharging

42:22.440 --> 42:23.220
all your obligations.

42:23.660 --> 42:25.340
It's the emergency exit

42:25.340 --> 42:25.880
that lets you

42:25.880 --> 42:26.600
leave the building

42:26.600 --> 42:27.740
without burning it down

42:27.740 --> 42:28.960
or leaving anyone behind.

42:29.420 --> 42:29.680
Yes.

42:30.000 --> 42:31.120
And this brings us

42:31.120 --> 42:31.960
to theorem 5

42:31.960 --> 42:33.000
the theorem

42:33.000 --> 42:34.240
of the excluded cut

42:34.240 --> 42:35.280
which defines

42:35.280 --> 42:36.480
exactly mathematically

42:36.480 --> 42:37.460
what it means

42:37.460 --> 42:38.040
to be trapped.

42:38.560 --> 42:39.520
If you were standing

42:39.520 --> 42:40.540
at a particular state

42:40.540 --> 42:41.280
on the whiteboard

42:41.280 --> 42:42.300
and there is

42:42.300 --> 42:43.320
absolutely no

42:43.320 --> 42:44.440
continuous path

42:44.440 --> 42:45.900
in the permitted graph

42:45.900 --> 42:46.400
that leads

42:46.400 --> 42:47.400
to a corrective state

42:47.400 --> 42:49.040
the theorem proves

42:49.040 --> 42:49.500
there must be

42:49.500 --> 42:50.000
a boundary

42:50.000 --> 42:51.000
a cut

42:51.000 --> 42:52.720
completely surrounding you.

42:53.340 --> 42:53.700
A cut

42:53.700 --> 42:54.620
in the graph.

42:55.020 --> 42:55.220
Yes.

42:55.600 --> 42:56.500
There is a perimeter

42:56.500 --> 42:57.280
drawn around

42:57.280 --> 42:58.120
your current state

42:58.120 --> 42:59.440
where every single line

42:59.440 --> 43:00.180
that leads outward

43:00.180 --> 43:00.980
towards correction

43:00.980 --> 43:02.400
has been explicitly

43:02.400 --> 43:03.160
identified

43:03.160 --> 43:04.340
and severed

43:04.340 --> 43:05.060
by the controller.

43:05.760 --> 43:07.060
It is a mathematical quarantine.

43:07.740 --> 43:09.440
It is a structural certificate

43:09.440 --> 43:10.720
that you are trapped.

43:11.460 --> 43:12.200
You are not trapped

43:12.200 --> 43:13.300
because you lack skill

43:13.300 --> 43:14.820
or because you've failed

43:14.820 --> 43:15.460
at execution

43:15.460 --> 43:17.020
but because the controller

43:17.020 --> 43:18.620
has methodically anticipated

43:18.620 --> 43:19.600
and destroyed

43:19.600 --> 43:20.760
every single exit path.

43:21.360 --> 43:22.260
But let me challenge this.

43:22.980 --> 43:23.840
What if the system

43:23.840 --> 43:24.880
has a built-in exit?

43:25.380 --> 43:26.380
Think about a driver

43:26.380 --> 43:27.780
for a gig economy app

43:27.780 --> 43:28.900
or even just a standard

43:28.900 --> 43:29.380
employment.

43:29.440 --> 43:31.200
There is literally

43:31.200 --> 43:32.300
a button on the app

43:32.300 --> 43:32.820
that says

43:32.820 --> 43:34.020
