46:54.520 --> 46:55.100
of approval

46:55.100 --> 46:56.240
or every time

46:56.240 --> 46:57.180
a new software update

46:57.180 --> 46:58.180
removes a manual

46:58.180 --> 46:59.080
override button

46:59.080 --> 47:01.180
a line is quietly

47:01.180 --> 47:02.560
erased from your graph.

47:03.500 --> 47:04.400
Your world of choices

47:04.400 --> 47:05.160
is shrinking

47:05.160 --> 47:06.380
one memo

47:06.380 --> 47:07.140
at a time.

47:07.140 --> 47:08.460
And theorems 9

47:08.460 --> 47:09.000
and 10

47:09.000 --> 47:09.980
turn this process

47:09.980 --> 47:10.840
into a mathematically

47:10.840 --> 47:11.540
measurable

47:11.540 --> 47:12.740
depletion horizon.

47:13.500 --> 47:13.900
They apply

47:13.900 --> 47:14.820
continuous measures

47:14.820 --> 47:15.580
like calculus

47:15.580 --> 47:17.080
and discrete counting

47:17.080 --> 47:18.460
to show a terrifying

47:18.460 --> 47:19.020
reality.

47:19.800 --> 47:20.200
If the rate

47:20.200 --> 47:21.040
at which your capacity

47:21.040 --> 47:22.380
to revise your purposes

47:22.380 --> 47:23.520
is being destroyed

47:23.520 --> 47:25.440
is consistently greater

47:25.440 --> 47:25.940
than the rate

47:25.940 --> 47:26.440
at which you are

47:26.440 --> 47:27.460
building new capacities

47:27.460 --> 47:28.980
you will inevitably

47:28.980 --> 47:29.600
hit zero.

47:30.300 --> 47:30.740
A finite

47:30.740 --> 47:31.720
depletion horizon.

47:32.180 --> 47:32.700
Your agency

47:32.700 --> 47:34.180
literally runs out

47:34.180 --> 47:34.760
like sand

47:34.760 --> 47:35.600
in an hourglass.

47:35.600 --> 47:36.820
It's strict

47:36.820 --> 47:38.000
mathematical bookkeeping.

47:38.420 --> 47:39.100
If the net rate

47:39.100 --> 47:40.200
of your revision capacity

47:40.200 --> 47:41.040
